# JSX inline-tag spacing

JSX line breaks around inline tags are not reliable spaces (`greenside`, `them).The`).
ESLint `local/jsx-inline-prose-spacing` is the gate (`npm run lint`).

Between preceding text and a following inline tag (`<strong>`, `<dfn>`, `<em>`, `<b>`, `<span>`, `<code>`, `<Link>`, etc.), use `{" "}` so the space is not lost across a line break (e.g. `The{" "}<strong>`). Same after a period/paren before a following tag. After a closing inline tag, if more text follows, use `{" "}` as well. Keep following punctuation on the same line as the closing tag (`</a>.` not `</a>` then `.` on the next line).

```tsx
The{" "}
<strong className="font-semibold text-slate-900">green</strong>
{" "}
side is the state&apos;s record.
```

Prefer `</strong>{" "}else` so formatters cannot drop the space. Re-read edited prose as plain text.
